{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Device - Okta Device Enrolled or Platform SSO Key Registered",
	"Description": "A device was enrolled, a device token was issued, or a Platform SSO key was registered. An enrolled device is a standing authenticator, so an adversary who gets one enrolled no longer needs the password or the original factor.\n\nEvent types: device.enrollment.create, device.token.enrollment.create, device.platform_sso.keys.register, device.local_account.create, device.password_sync.enrollment.create, device.desktop_mfa.enrollment.create\n\nReference(s):\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/api/openapi/okta-management/management/tag/SystemLog/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "eb6aa441-0399-572b-a65d-2bc6c2416d4e",
